---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config.mjs';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy — The Critical Point (fncuthdert.com)" lang="en">
  <article class="post">
    <h1 class="post-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="post-content legal">
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {SITE.legalUpdatedEn}</p>
      <p>This policy explains how "{SITE.nameEn}" (fncuthdert.com — the "Site") handles your information. The Site is designed to <strong>collect as little data as possible</strong>: there are no usernames or passwords, no registration, and reading free content requires no personal information.</p>

      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Payment information</strong>: tips, article purchases and memberships are completed in PayPal's window. Your card details and PayPal password are processed directly by PayPal and <strong>never pass through or get stored on this Site's servers</strong>. From PayPal we receive the transaction status, amount, order or subscription ID, and your PayPal account email.</li>
        <li><strong>Membership records</strong>: when you subscribe, the Site stores your subscription ID, tier, PayPal email and access period, to decide which content you can read and to verify you when you restore access on another device. Topic requests from Inner Circle members are stored so we can reply.</li>
        <li><strong>Functional cookies</strong>: unlocking a single article sets a cookie whose name starts with u_ (valid for one year); members get a cookie named m. They only remember "unlocked" or "member" and are not used for tracking or profiling. The Site uses no advertising or analytics cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Server logs</strong>: the Site is hosted on Cloudflare, which keeps basic access logs (such as IP address and access time) for security and operations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
      <p>The above is used solely to complete and verify payments, deliver paid content, handle refunds and disputes, and keep the Site secure. We do not sell or rent your information, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

      <h2>3. Third-party services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>PayPal (payment processing): <a href="https://www.paypal.com/myaccount/privacy/privacyhub" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PayPal Privacy Hub</a></li>
        <li>Stripe (payments made before November 2026): <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">stripe.com/privacy</a></li>
        <li>Cloudflare (hosting and delivery): <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a></li>
        <li>Google Fonts (font loading)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Data retention</h2>
      <p>Transaction records are retained per PayPal's policies and applicable law. Membership records are kept for one year after a subscription ends, to handle refunds and disputes. You may clear the cookies at any time and restore access on the Subscribe page with your order or subscription ID.</p>

      <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of information we hold about you (except transaction records we are legally required to keep). Contact <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> and we will respond within a reasonable time.</p>

      <h2>6. Minors</h2>
      <p>The Site is intended for adult readers. We do not knowingly collect personal information from minors.</p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>Revisions to this policy will be posted on this page with an updated date.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>Operator: {SITE.operator}<br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
